[l_english.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL]
Steel Chariot (Armored Vehicle)

[l_english.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL_desc]
Wait, you do realize that this is escentially a wagon, right? It is pulled by a pony. So why would a pony army becomes faster when they added a heavy and useless piece of steel to be pulled in their division?
§g“I guess the gravity should take all the credits when you are marching downhill. Definitely not because their commanders are too lazy to walk faster.”§!

[l_english.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL_short]
Steel Chariot

[l_simp_chinese.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL]
铁制战车 (装甲载具)

[l_simp_chinese.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL_desc]
等等，你应该意识到了这本质上是一辆马车，对吧？它是由一匹马拉着的。那么为什么一支小马组成的军队，在他们的军团里加入了一块需要被拉动的沉重而无用的铁皮后会变得更快呢？
§g“我猜是重力的原因，你们下坡的时候。绝对不是因为军队的领导者们不愿意自己走太快。”§!

[l_simp_chinese.EQUIPMENT_VEHICLE_STEEL_short]
铁制战车
